   "speech": "Before him, to and fro, in a motley succession of clothes and faces, passed a multitude of city folk. In this enormous city, seething with a lava of passions (greed, anger, cunning, fear, thousand-hued desires, bewilderment and insolence), Ranum endured the keen torments of a spirit that strives toward the repose of blissful contemplation, yet is compelled to dwell amid the filth, blood and darkness of imperfect beings passing through their lower incarnations. The hell of war and the social earthquake hindered him in performing his inner work. The contagion of the mood of millions, perceptible to any townsman, penetrated Ranum with immeasurably greater force, for the slightest attention of his refined power allowed him to read thoughts; more than that, to know the whole hidden essence of a human personality.",
